-- title:
--   The exceptional fibre budget is one above binary rank
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group, $H=G[2]$, $K=G[3]$, and $P_\chi(S)=\sum_{x\in S}\chi(x)$ for a complex additive character $\chi$ (so $\chi(x+y)=\chi(x)\chi(y)$). Write $Q_S$ for ordered-sum counts and $\mathcal O_B(S)=(Q_S,(P_{\chi_i}(S))_i)$ for a bank $B=(\chi_i)$. Assume $G$ finite, $|H|=2^r$, and a support $S$ has $|F(S)|=2|H|$. Then its defined fibre budget is $$b_F(S)=r+1.$$ There is no separately stated three-element premise on $S$.
-- source:
